# Vendored, PATCHED Livox-SDK2 (task A3).
#
# The SDK source is NOT committed. It is reproducible from two things that
# ARE committed: fetch_sdk2.sh (pinned tarball URL) and patches/ (the three
# unified diffs S2 proved are required). Same policy the S2 spike used
# (spikes/s2-mid360-sim/.gitignore), for the same reasons: the upstream tree
# is ~9 MB of third-party source, its licence is MIT but its provenance is a
# GitHub branch tarball, and vendoring the diff rather than the tree makes
# "what did we change and why" reviewable in four screens instead of none.
#
# Bootstrap:  engine/third_party/fetch_sdk2.sh
Livox-SDK2/

# Vendored, PATCHED Livox-SDK **v1** (task A17, the Mid-70's SDK).
#
# Same policy as SDK2 above, same two committed artefacts: fetch_sdk1.sh
# (pinned tarball URL) and patches/sdk1-*.patch (the three diffs the S8 spike
# proved are required — CMake floor, -Werror, and the ${PROJECT_NAME}_static
# target name). Note the directory is "Livox-SDK", not "Livox-SDK1": that is
# what upstream's repo is called.
#
# Bootstrap:  engine/third_party/fetch_sdk1.sh
Livox-SDK/
